kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[7]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  modify_requirement,tui1,"line-array-differential-render","The TUI MUST render using a self-built differential render engine over a line-array screen representation (previous_lines vs new_lines per-frame diff, writing only changed lines wrapped in synchronized output CSI 2026), driven by crossterm directly for raw mode/events/cursor. The TUI MUST NOT use ratatui (cell-grid Buffer, immediate-mode Widget trait, Viewport::Inline, or insert_before). The engine owns the whole conversation history as a single Vec of styled lines; streaming appends new lines via diff (no irreversible commit, no mutable-tail/scrollback split). Evidence: pi-tui line-array + retained-widget model (skill tui-pro-of-pi-tui rendering-engine.md); the prior ratatui inline-viewport model forced commit-unit = render-unit = paragraph, losing cross-paragraph markdown context (the c396 screenshot root cause).",null,null,null
  modify_requirement,tui12,"line-array-render-pipeline","The TUI MUST render via a per-frame pipeline: widget tree render(width) produces a flat Vec of StyledLine (the whole conversation), the engine diffs against previous_lines by line equality, picks one of three strategies (first render without clearing, full redraw with clearing, normal diff with line clear + rewrite), wraps writes in synchronized output, positions a virtual IME cursor, and saves state. The hard width invariant MUST fire on both the diff path AND the full-redraw path (an over-wide line is a hard error, not silent wrap). Evidence: skill rendering-engine.md Steps 4-6; the prior insert_before + Viewport::Inline(TAIL_HEIGHT) model split mutable tail from scrollback irreversibly.",null,null,null
  modify_requirement,tui41,"virtual-terminal-test-harness","The TUI rendering layer MUST be covered by an in-memory virtual terminal cell-grid harness (feed the engine's ANSI output stream, assert on cell content, cursor position, and styles per row), covering at minimum: the per-frame diff path (append-only growth, in-place edit, width change full redraw, shrink orphan-row clearing), streaming text wrapping at terminal width (CJK-aware), and clean exit. This replaces the prior ratatui TestBackend harness (which asserted on ratatui Buffer cells and is unavailable once ratatui is removed). Evidence: skill terminal-foundations.md testing-strategy (headless terminal emulator as VirtualTerminal); pi-tui uses @xterm/headless.",null,null,null
  modify_requirement,tui50,"streaming-via-line-array-append","The TUI streaming render MUST grow the in-progress assistant text by appending new rendered lines to the line-array (the engine diffs and writes only the new lines, scrolling the viewport to follow the end). The mutable region and the scrollback are a single unified line-array (no two-region split, no irreversible commit). The whole accumulated turn source is re-rendered each frame so cross-paragraph markdown context (block blank-line spacing, list/blockquote prefix continuity) is preserved. TurnEnd flushes the residual tail (already in the line-array; just marks streaming done). Evidence: skill rendering-engine.md Step 5 normal diff append case; the prior two-region (mutable last line + irreversible insert_before scrollback) model forced the c377 fence-aware paragraph hack and lost cross-paragraph context.",null,null,null
  modify_requirement,tui70,"self-research-markdown-line-array","The TUI markdown rendering MUST be backed by the self-researched lightweight renderer (pulldown-cmark + syntect, no box-drawing borders/tree-connectors/table-lines), producing the engine's native StyledLine type (not ratatui Line) so it integrates directly into the line-array diff. Code blocks use syntect highlighting without background/border/language-label. The MarkdownStyle adapter (for_user/for_assistant/for_thinking) remains the single seam. Tables render as tab/space-aligned plain text (no Unicode border characters) so copy-paste yields clean low-token markdown. Evidence: skill ui-components.md Markdown widget + D6 token-economy principle; c395/c396 styling carries over (heading grading, blockquote greater-than prefix, ordered-list number marker).",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui82,"engine-width-contract","The TUI differential render engine MUST enforce a hard width contract: every StyledLine produced by a widget MUST have display width less than or equal to the render width, checked on BOTH the normal-diff write path AND the full-redraw path. An over-wide line MUST abort with a diagnostic (width, offending line, crash log) rather than silently wrapping and desyncing every subsequent diff row. Width utilities MUST be ANSI-aware (SGR/OSC sequences count zero width) and wide-char-aware (CJK/emoji count width 2, combining marks count 0). Evidence: skill rendering-engine.md Step 6 + audit.md Finding 2 (pi-tui only checks the diff path; the port must check both).",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui83,"engine-resize-adaptive","The TUI MUST handle terminal resize (window size change AND font zoom changing rows/columns) by treating any width change as a full redraw (wrapping changes every line) and any height change as a full redraw (to keep the viewport aligned), rebuilding the widget tree at the new width and re-diffing. Resize MUST NOT lose content, lose the input cursor, corrupt the streaming state, or leave orphan characters at line ends. The Event::Resize from crossterm MUST trigger a render frame (not be ignored). Evidence: skill rendering-engine.md Step 5B full redraw on width/height change + Step 8 viewport math; the prior model ignored Event::Resize (mod.rs let Event::Key(_) = ev else continue dropped it) and could not re-wrap committed scrollback.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[9]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui1,"no-ratatui-dependency","the Cargo.toml and tui source are inspected","the dependency list and import statements are checked","ratatui-core, ratatui-crossterm, and ratatui-widgets are absent from the tui feature; no source file imports ratatui_core or ratatui_crossterm"
  tui1,"line-array-diff-append","the TUI is streaming an assistant reply that appends a new line each frame","the engine renders a frame","only the newly-appended line(s) are written to the terminal (previous unchanged lines are not rewritten) and the terminal scrolls to follow the end without scrollback pollution"
  tui12,"width-change-full-redraw","the terminal is resized narrower then wider while the TUI is running","a render frame occurs after each resize","a full redraw is performed (all lines re-wrapped at the new width) with no horizontal artifacts and no orphan characters at line ends"
  tui41,"virtual-terminal-covers-diff","the engine is fed an append-only sequence then an in-place edit then a width change via the virtual terminal harness","the harness cell-grid is asserted","each case produces the expected cells (only new line on append, only changed line on in-place edit, full rewrite on width change) and the cursor ends at the expected position"
  tui50,"streaming-preserves-cross-paragraph-context","an assistant reply containing a paragraph followed by a fenced code block is streamed one delta at a time","the engine renders frames during streaming","the blank-line spacing between the paragraph and the code block renders correctly (the renderer saw the full document via per-frame full-source render) without a paragraph-split hack"
  tui70,"markdown-table-copyable","an assistant reply containing a GFM table is rendered and the terminal is selected-and-copied","the copied text is inspected","the table is tab or space aligned plain text without Unicode border characters so the copy is clean low-token markdown"
  tui82,"hard-width-error-on-overflow","a widget returns a StyledLine whose display width exceeds the render width","the engine attempts to render the frame","the engine aborts with a diagnostic (rather than silently wrapping and desyncing the diff)"
  tui83,"resize-event-triggers-render","the user resizes the terminal while a turn is streaming","the crossterm Event::Resize is delivered","a render frame is scheduled at the new dimensions and the content re-flows without losing the streaming tail or the input cursor"
  tui83,"font-zoom-handled","the user changes the terminal font size (changing rows and columns) while the TUI is idle","a render frame occurs","the layout reflows to the new dimensions and no content is lost or corrupted"
